(A library that appends to, or frees, a list it is handed. A list freed on
 one side of the boundary is empty and refuses writes on the other, and a
 second `Free` on the other side is refused too, never unmapping the
 program's own memory.)
Library shelf version "1.0".

To 'add to' with a list called items.
    append "added" to items.

To 'drop' with a list called items.
    Free items.
